{"body":"Agents that implement `agent.TranscriptPreparer` (e.g., OpenCode) may need `PrepareTranscript` to materialize/refresh the transcript file before it exists on disk. `resolveAndValidateTranscript` currently stats the path immediately, so `entire attach --agent opencode <id>` will fail even when the session is valid. Consider calling `PrepareTranscript(ctx, transcriptPath)` (best-effort) before the `os.Stat` check.","created_at":"2026-03-17T21:20:15Z","id":2949628174,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":316,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/attach.go","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This branch appends a new `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer even when the commit message already contains one. That can create duplicate checkpoint trailers on repeated `attach` runs, and it contradicts the PR description’s “no-op if trailer already exists” behavior. If `ParseCheckpoint` finds a valid existing trailer, skip amending (or replace the existing trailer instead of adding another).
","created_at":"2026-03-17T21:20:15Z","id":2949628191,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":380,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/attach.go","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"The fallback transcript lookup walks *all* directories under the agent’s global base dir (e.g. `~/.claude/projects`, `~/.gemini/tmp`). This differs from the PR description (scoped to repo-root subdirectories) and can be both slow and overly broad (risking attaching a transcript from an unrelated project). Consider narrowing the search scope (repo-derived project dirs only) or limiting recursion to the agent’s known directory structure.","created_at":"2026-03-17T21:20:15Z","id":2949628206,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":77,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/transcript.go","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"This test relies on the transcript being missing, but when the primary lookup fails the new fallback search will walk the real `~/.claude/projects` directory (it doesn’t respect `ENTIRE_TEST_CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`). That makes the test non-hermetic and potentially flaky on dev machines. Set `HOME` to a temp dir in this test (as the Gemini subdir test does), or add a test override for the fallback search so it never touches the real home directory.","created_at":"2026-03-17T21:20:16Z","id":2949628234,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":44,"path":"cmd/entire/cli/attach_test.go","user":"Copilot"}
